{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And I bore you on eagles' wings.</b> Rashi explains: this is the day they came to Raamses. And if you ask: but above, in the pericope of Bo, Rashi explained that it was the day they came from Raamses to Succot — one may answer that <b>and I bore you</b> refers to this and refers to that." "<b>On eagles' wings.</b> In the sea. Like a bird flying and carrying its fledglings over the river, in the manner of flight."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The phrase 'refers to this and refers to that' means the verse applies to both events mentioned by Rashi."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:40.497841931Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}